Deephaven Sample Data
Copyright (c) 2016-2026 Deephaven Data Labs and Patent Pending

This product includes datasets from third parties, vendored in
src/deephaven/sample_data/_data. The CSV files were exported unmodified from the
copies bundled with the plotly Python package (https://github.com/plotly/plotly.py),
version 6.9.0, which is licensed under the MIT License reproduced at the end of this
file. The original sources and licenses of each dataset are listed below. The
functions in deephaven.sample_data rename columns and add synthetic ticking rows.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
iris.csv

Source: UCI Machine Learning Repository, "Iris" dataset
(https://archive.ics.uci.edu/dataset/53/iris), donated 1988.
Original measurements: Fisher, R.A. (1936), "The use of multiple measurements in
taxonomic problems", Annals of Eugenics, 7(2), 179-188.
Licensed under CC BY 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/).

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
tips.csv

Source: Bryant, P. G. and Smith, M. (1995), Practical Data Analysis: Case Studies
in Business Statistics, Richard D. Irwin Publishing.
Redistributed via the reshape2 R package (Hadley Wickham, MIT License) and Rdatasets
(https://vincentarelbundock.github.io/Rdatasets/doc/reshape2/tips.html).
The original authors publish no explicit data license; this dataset is included
based on its long-standing open redistribution by reshape2, seaborn-data, Rdatasets
and plotly.

